; Module-definition file for d3d9.dll (Vireio Perception v5 DxProxy).
; The DLL masquerades as d3d9.dll — it's renamed/dropped next to a DX9
; game's exe and Windows's DLL-search-order loads it instead of the
; system one. We forward to %SystemRoot%\System32\d3d9.dll inside
; Direct3DCreate9 / Direct3DCreate9Ex.

; Module-definition file for the v5 d3d9.dll proxy. Both entry points
; wrap and forward to the system d3d9.dll (loaded by Main.cpp's LoadDll()
; from %SystemRoot%\System32\). Games that use IDirect3D9Ex (Skyrim SE
; launcher, some UE3 titles) load via Direct3DCreate9Ex; everything else
; uses Direct3DCreate9.
;
; D3DPERF_* functions are PIX-debugger no-ops in modern Windows; included
; to keep the export shape compatible with games that GetProcAddress them.
EXPORTS
    Direct3DCreate9          @1
    Direct3DCreate9Ex        @2
    D3DPERF_BeginEvent       @3
    D3DPERF_EndEvent         @4
    D3DPERF_SetMarker        @5
    D3DPERF_SetRegion        @6
    D3DPERF_QueryRepeatFrame @7
    D3DPERF_SetOptions       @8
    D3DPERF_GetStatus        @9
